Package: pve-triton-virglrenderer
Architecture: amd64
# System install (prefix /usr): QEMU (pve-qemu-kvm with the Triton quilt
# series) links libvirglrenderer.so.1 by soname at build and run time, and
# PVE launches /usr/bin/kvm directly with no wrapper, so the Neptune-capable
# library must BE the system libvirglrenderer — hence Conflicts/Replaces of
# the Debian 1.1.0 packages (same soname; Neptune is a superset).
# Provides are versioned so that versioned dependencies (including this
# package's own ${shlibs:Depends} on libvirglrenderer1, emitted because the
# render server links the soname shipped in the same package) resolve
# against the virtual package; unversioned Provides cannot satisfy (>= N).
Provides: libvirglrenderer1 (= ${binary:Version}), libvirglrenderer-dev (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: libvirglrenderer1, libvirglrenderer-dev, virglrenderer
Replaces: libvirglrenderer1, libvirglrenderer-dev, virglrenderer
# Optional but required for Intel/AMD hosts: mesa-vulkan-drivers provides
# the ANV/RADV ICD the render server's DXVK libraries target (D3D11 ->
# Vulkan). Kept a Recommends, not a Depends, so an NVIDIA host can satisfy
# the Vulkan requirement with the proprietary driver's ICD instead.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, pve-triton-dxvk, libvulkan1
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers
Description: virglrenderer with Neptune D3D11 render server (Triton stack)
 Fork of utmapp/virglrenderer (dev/neptune-linux branch) built with
 -Dneptune=true -Dvenus=true. Provides the virgl_render_server which
 deserializes Neptune D3D11 API calls from QEMU virtio-gpu and executes
 them on the host via the pve-triton-dxvk libraries. Installs to the
 normal /usr paths and takes over libvirglrenderer from Debian.
 Upstream: https://github.com/utmapp/virglrenderer
